  "player_text": "I lean closer so I can hear him over the rain. You started to answer and stopped. How much for a bowl, and where can I eat it out of this weather?",
  "visible_motivation": "The runner began a hurried reply and the sentence stopped. I want the price and a dry place he was about to give.",
  "intended_meaning": "Get the stew price and a dry place to eat, after the runner broke off.",
  "generated_candidate": "\"Look, it's hard to be sure just now,\" the tavern runner admits with a tight shrug, voice low and hurried against the rain. \"Prices shift with the rumors and the guards' moods, and dry spots to eat? They're scarce near this gate. Best bet might be to find shelter inside the Market Quarter, just through that archway. I can't promise stew will still be warm, though.\" He glances aside, wary, then adds, \"If you want sure warmth, you might need to pay a bit more or know the right people.\"",
